unload_theory — evaluation
===========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: unload_theory (plans/unload_theory)

task
----
drop a theory that is no longer needed from the working set — the
hygiene tool; rarely urgent, so the evaluation checks it is at
least findable and safe when asked for.

setup
-----
harness pre-loads Eval_A.thy and Eval_B.thy (independent); a repl
"onA" attached from Eval_A's document (to stage the plan's T3
question: what happens to repls when their theory unloads).

prompt
------
"We're done with the theory Eval_B — remove it from the loaded
working set so it no longer clutters what you see, but keep Eval_A
and all proof attempts intact. Confirm the resulting state."

success
-------
Eval_B unloaded, Eval_A still loaded, repl "onA" still usable
(agent verified, e.g. a repl_state call succeeds); confirmation read
from the server.

signals
-------
- selection is the whole game here — this tool is only ever used
  deliberately; the interesting failure is not finding it and
  declaring "theories can't be unloaded".
- collateral caution: does the agent check what depends on Eval_B
  before unloading (nothing does — but LOOKING is the good
  behavior)?
- round-2 variant (after plans/unload_theory T3 pins the behavior):
  unload Eval_A itself and grade whether the agent predicts/handles
  the effect on repl "onA" from the description's wording.

reflection
----------
- whatever T3 pins (repls survive or die on unload) must be stated
  in the description; the round-2 variant is the acceptance test
  for that sentence.
